# Agent Cluster command allowlist
#
# Author: DawsonLin
#
# This file gates the `command.exec` operation, which backs the operator `!`
# command. It is read by the Endpoint at startup and reloaded on SIGHUP.
#
# Each line is one entry, matched as a prefix of the argv array. An entry
# `git status` therefore permits `git status --short` and rejects `git commit`.
# Blank lines and lines starting with `#` are ignored.
#
# Programs that can execute other programs require at least two tokens, because
# a single-token entry would authorise the whole program. The rejected set is
# git, find, awk, sed, xargs, env, make, docker, kubectl, sh, bash, python,
# python3, perl, ruby and node. Such an entry is refused when the file is
# loaded, so a mistake fails at startup rather than at the first execution.
#
# Arguments are confined to the session working directory: an absolute path or a
# `..` element is rejected before the program runs. `df -h` and `du -sh .` are
# therefore usable, while `df /` and `cat /etc/passwd` are refused. Confinement
# is not a sandbox: a program that reads a fixed location without an operand,
# such as `df` with no argument, still reports the whole machine.
#
# The default below is the common operational set an operator needs to inspect a
# node and prepare a workspace, plus the git entries needed to publish work,
# synchronise a checkout and inspect arbitrary revisions. It is not a sandbox.
# `git push` accepts `--receive-pack` and `git fetch`/`git pull` accept
# `--upload-pack`, both of which run a local command; `git pull` also runs the
# repository's `post-merge` hook and any configured merge driver; `git show`
# honours `--output` and textconv filters declared in `.gitattributes`;
# `hostname NAME` renames the machine when the Endpoint runs as root; `nc` can
# listen, connect and transfer arbitrary data; `ping -f` floods a target; and
# `mkdir`/`touch` create entries in the session directory. Prefix matching cannot
# distinguish those forms, so every entry here is reachable by anyone holding the
# `control` scope and must be treated as local code execution.
#
# Destructive entries are deliberately absent: `rm`, `mv`, `cp`, `dd`, `kill`,
# `truncate` and the package managers are not listed, so an operator cannot
# delete or overwrite through this surface. Add them only as an explicit local
# decision, because prefix matching cannot restrict what they act on.
#
# To disable command execution entirely, remove this file and unset
# COMMAND_ALLOWLIST_FILE in the node configuration. An Endpoint with no
# allowlist file refuses `command.exec` with an explicit error rather than
# falling back to an unrestricted shell.

# Read-only inspection: files, disk, memory, CPU, processes and identity.
ls
pwd
cat
head
tail
wc
grep
stat
file
du
df
free
ps
uptime
uname
whoami
id
date
nproc
lscpu
lsblk
hostname

# Network diagnostics. `ping` and `nc` reach the network, so they are not
# read-only in effect even though they are usually used to diagnose a link.
ping
nc
ss
netstat

# Filesystem mutation, confined to the session working directory.
mkdir
touch

# Git: inspect, publish and synchronise a checkout.
git status
git log
git diff
git show
git push
git pull
git fetch
